WEBVTT

00:00:14.008 --> 00:00:15.488
(CHEERING)

00:00:20.808 --> 00:00:22.408
Princess Vanellope?

00:00:22.568 --> 00:00:24.488
Now I remember.

00:00:25.688 --> 00:00:29.968
All hail the rightful ruler
of Sugar Rush...

00:00:30.168 --> 00:00:31.768
Princess Vanellope.

00:00:32.008 --> 00:00:33.008
(GASPS)

00:00:33.088 --> 00:00:34.728
I remember. She's our princess!

00:00:34.808 --> 00:00:36.048
Oh, that's right!

00:00:36.208 --> 00:00:38.008
We are so sorry
about the way we treated you.

00:00:38.168 --> 00:00:39.608
Yeah, those were jokes!

00:00:39.768 --> 00:00:42.528
(WHINING) I was just doing
what Taffyta told me to do!

00:00:43.328 --> 00:00:44.408
Tut-tut.

00:00:44.568 --> 00:00:48.088
As your merciful princess,
I hereby decree

00:00:48.288 --> 00:00:52.688
that everyone who was ever
mean to me shall be

00:00:53.128 --> 00:00:54.168
executed.

00:00:54.328 --> 00:00:56.688
What? No, please!

00:00:56.808 --> 00:00:58.088
Oh, my land.

00:00:58.168 --> 00:01:00.408
Oh! This place just got interesting.

00:01:00.528 --> 00:01:02.768
(SOBBING) I don't want to die!

00:01:02.888 --> 00:01:06.448
I'm just kidding. Stop crying, Taffyta.

00:01:06.648 --> 00:01:08.448
I'm trying, but it won't stop.

00:01:09.768 --> 00:01:11.128
Wow.

00:01:11.288 --> 00:01:14.408
So this is the real you. Princess.

00:01:14.568 --> 00:01:18.488
Aw, Ralph, what are you, nuts?
Come on. This isn't me.

00:01:20.128 --> 00:01:22.048
This is me.

00:01:22.368 --> 00:01:23.648
Huh?

00:01:23.728 --> 00:01:25.328
Look, the code may say I'm a princess

00:01:25.408 --> 00:01:27.008
but I know who I really am, Ralph,

00:01:27.128 --> 00:01:30.248
I'm a racer with
the greatest superpower ever.

00:01:30.408 --> 00:01:31.808
I was here, I was there.

00:01:32.008 --> 00:01:33.808
I was glitching through the walls.

00:01:33.928 --> 00:01:34.968
I'm not giving that up.

00:01:35.048 --> 00:01:37.168
Um, pardon me for asking,

00:01:37.408 --> 00:01:40.408
but without a princess,
who's going to lead us?

00:01:40.488 --> 00:01:41.528
Yeah. Who?

00:01:42.488 --> 00:01:45.408
Uh, me.
I'm thinking more along the lines of

00:01:45.488 --> 00:01:47.688
a constitutional democracy.

00:01:47.848 --> 00:01:51.208
President Vanellope von Schweetz.

00:01:51.328 --> 00:01:53.008
Has a nice ring to it, don't you think?

00:01:54.288 --> 00:01:56.928
Fix-It, Wreck-It,
the arcade's about to open.

00:01:57.088 --> 00:01:58.928
Let's move 'em out.

00:02:06.008 --> 00:02:09.168
You could just stay here
and live in the castle.

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:10.568
You'd have your own wing

00:02:10.648 --> 00:02:12.408
where no one would ever
complain about your stench

00:02:12.568 --> 00:02:14.488
or treat you bad ever again.

00:02:14.648 --> 00:02:16.568
You could be happy.

00:02:17.368 --> 00:02:19.728
I'm already happy.

00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:21.768
I've got the coolest friend in the world.

00:02:22.688 --> 00:02:24.848
And besides, I've got a job to do, too.

00:02:25.368 --> 00:02:28.648
It may not be as fancy
as being president

00:02:28.768 --> 00:02:30.088
but it's my duty.

00:02:30.248 --> 00:02:31.808
And it's a big duty!

00:02:32.208 --> 00:02:33.528
(CHUCKLES)

00:02:33.848 --> 00:02:34.968
Ralph, are you coming, brother?

00:02:36.488 --> 00:02:39.168
See you later, President Fart Feathers.

00:02:39.368 --> 00:02:42.328
Au revoir, Admiral Underpants.

00:02:42.728 --> 00:02:45.728
And farewell, Baroness Boogerface.

00:02:45.848 --> 00:02:48.168
Goodbye, Major Body Odor!

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:50.608
-Hasta la vista, you...
-Ralph!

00:02:50.808 --> 00:02:53.168
-All right. To be continued.
-Yeah!

00:02:53.248 --> 00:02:54.928
ALL: Hooray!

00:03:07.328 --> 00:03:08.488
RALPH: I'm gonna wreck it!

00:03:08.848 --> 00:03:10.048
(GRUNTING ANGRILY)

00:03:10.368 --> 00:03:13.608
Hey! Ralph's back! Isn't that great!

00:03:14.488 --> 00:03:16.248
(LAUGHS EXCITEDLY)
The gang's all here!

00:03:16.328 --> 00:03:20.608
So, I'm happy to report,
and you'll be happy to hear,

00:03:20.688 --> 00:03:22.328
I'm taking life one game at a time.

00:03:22.488 --> 00:03:24.728
All right! Yeah, Ralph!

00:03:24.848 --> 00:03:26.368
RALPH: Of course,
the job hasn't changed.

00:03:27.448 --> 00:03:31.128
But, news flash,
the Nicelanders are being nice to me!

00:03:32.328 --> 00:03:35.528
And that got me thinking about
those poor guys left without a game.

00:03:36.168 --> 00:03:38.168
-So here's what we did.
-We're gonna wreck it!

00:03:38.328 --> 00:03:40.528
We asked them to help us out
on the bonus levels.

00:03:41.488 --> 00:03:42.648
We can fix it!

00:03:43.368 --> 00:03:44.368
RALPH: I'm telling you, guys,

00:03:44.448 --> 00:03:46.288
we haven't been this popular in years.

00:03:46.408 --> 00:03:47.648
-It's crazy.
-Wow!

00:03:48.488 --> 00:03:50.248
The gamers say we're "retro,"

00:03:50.328 --> 00:03:53.208
which I think means "old but cool."

00:03:53.328 --> 00:03:54.768
BOY: How come
we never noticed this game?

00:03:54.888 --> 00:03:56.768
RALPH: Oh, and I decided
that living in the dump

00:03:56.848 --> 00:03:58.488
wasn't making me feel very good,

00:03:59.888 --> 00:04:01.128
so I cleaned it up,
built myself a little shack

00:04:01.208 --> 00:04:02.848
and a couple for the new guys, too.

00:04:02.928 --> 00:04:04.008
(MUTTERS)

00:04:04.088 --> 00:04:07.288
Well, with a little help from Felix. Oh!

00:04:07.608 --> 00:04:09.728
And guess who was the best man
at his and Calhoun's wedding.

00:04:10.488 --> 00:04:13.048
That's right, my friends,
old Ham Hands himself.

00:04:13.808 --> 00:04:15.728
Very elegant affair.
You should've seen it.

00:04:15.808 --> 00:04:17.288
Lot of grandeur.

00:04:17.368 --> 00:04:18.808
And not a single bug.

00:04:22.688 --> 00:04:26.248
Let's just say, some tears were shed.

00:04:28.008 --> 00:04:31.488
But I got to say, the best part of my day

00:04:31.688 --> 00:04:33.408
is when I get thrown off the roof.

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:37.048
Because when the Nicelanders
lift me up,

00:04:38.288 --> 00:04:40.608
I get a perfect view of Sugar Rush.

00:04:41.168 --> 00:04:42.688
And I can see Vanellope racing.

00:04:45.488 --> 00:04:46.488
Yes!

00:04:47.528 --> 00:04:48.888
RALPH: The kid's a natural.

00:04:49.848 --> 00:04:52.008
And the players love her, glitch and all.

00:04:52.688 --> 00:04:54.168
Just like I knew they would.

00:04:56.088 --> 00:04:58.888
Turns out I don't need a medal
to tell me I'm a good guy.

00:05:00.648 --> 00:05:02.648
'Cause if that little kid likes me...

00:05:06.288 --> 00:05:07.768
How bad can I be?

00:05:12.608 --> 00:05:13.848
(COIN DROPPING)

00:05:13.928 --> 00:05:15.248
(BEEPING)

00:05:24.528 --> 00:05:28.128
Switch on the sky
and the stars glow for you

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:31.928
Go see the world
'cause it's all so brand new

00:05:32.008 --> 00:05:36.008
Don't close your eyes
'cause your future's ready to shine

00:05:36.168 --> 00:05:39.808
It's just a matter of time
before we learn how to fly

00:05:41.128 --> 00:05:44.488
Welcome to the rhythm of the night

00:05:44.568 --> 00:05:48.168
There's something in the air
you can't deny

00:05:48.928 --> 00:05:49.928
(MUTTERING)

00:05:53.328 --> 00:05:56.328
It's been fun but now I've got to go

00:05:57.008 --> 00:05:59.688
Life is way too short to take it slow

00:06:00.808 --> 00:06:03.768
But before I go and hit the road

00:06:04.768 --> 00:06:09.528
I gotta know, 'til then
when can we do this again?

00:06:11.568 --> 00:06:13.648
When can I see you again?

00:06:15.328 --> 00:06:17.528
When can we do this again?

00:06:20.168 --> 00:06:24.688
I gotta know
when can I see you again?

